{"type":"assistant","uuid":"f5ac610e-ac7e-4f9a-80db-3a13f6306685","session_id":"2b03198c-6dc1-44c7-8cc7-d86c8bfbb378","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"f5ac610e-ac7e-4f9a-80db-3a13f6306685","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The build was successful. Let me now create a summary of the fix.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"978e551f-47c8-458d-b247-7161671172a6","session_id":"2b03198c-6dc1-44c7-8cc7-d86c8bfbb378","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"978e551f-47c8-458d-b247-7161671172a6","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe build is successful. Here's a summary of the fix:\n\n## Bug Analysis\n\n**Root Cause**: When a user enters an invalid Base32 secret (like \"test\") in the \"Enter details\" dialog, the `Entry` constructors call `Base32.decode()` without any error handling. The Apache Commons Codec library throws an `IllegalArgumentException` when the input contains characters that are not valid Base32 alphabet or produce invalid padding. This unhandled exception crashes the app.\n\n**Stack trace location**: The crash originates from `Entry.java:90` (one of the constructors) called via `ManualEntryDialog.java:210` (the \"Save\" button handler).\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. Added error string (`app/src/main/res/values/strings_main.xml`)\nAdded a new string resource for the error message:\n```xml\n<string name=\"toast_invalid_secret\">Invalid secret. Please check your input.</string>\n```\n\n### 2. Fixed crash in dialog (`app/src/main/java/org/shadowice/flocke/andotp/Dialogs/ManualEntryDialog.java`)\n- Added `import android.widget.Toast;`\n- Wrapped the entry creation logic in the \"Save\" button handler with a `try-catch` block that catches `IllegalArgumentException`\n- On catch, shows the error Toast message instead of crashing\n\nThe fix preserves all existing functionality while gracefully handling invalid Base32 input by displaying an error message to the user."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38240,"output_tokens":324,"cache_read_input_tokens":35632,"total_tokens":38564}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"97e5937b-88c0-47c0-aa59-bb54f66f93cc","session_id":"2b03198c-6dc1-44c7-8cc7-d86c8bfbb378","is_error":false,"duration_ms":49598,"duration_api_ms":21963,"num_turns":11,"result":"\n\nThe build is successful. Here's a summary of the fix:\n\n## Bug Analysis\n\n**Root Cause**: When a user enters an invalid Base32 secret (like \"test\") in the \"Enter details\" dialog, the `Entry` constructors call `Base32.decode()` without any error handling. The Apache Commons Codec library throws an `IllegalArgumentException` when the input contains characters that are not valid Base32 alphabet or produce invalid padding. This unhandled exception crashes the app.\n\n**Stack trace location**: The crash originates from `Entry.java:90` (one of the constructors) called via `ManualEntryDialog.java:210` (the \"Save\" button handler).\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. Added error string (`app/src/main/res/values/strings_main.xml`)\nAdded a new string resource for the error message:\n```xml\n<string name=\"toast_invalid_secret\">Invalid secret. Please check your input.</string>\n```\n\n### 2. Fixed crash in dialog (`app/src/main/java/org/shadowice/flocke/andotp/Dialogs/ManualEntryDialog.java`)\n- Added `import android.widget.Toast;`\n- Wrapped the entry creation logic in the \"Save\" button handler with a `try-catch` block that catches `IllegalArgumentException`\n- On catch, shows the error Toast message instead of crashing\n\nThe fix preserves all existing functionality while gracefully handling invalid Base32 input by displaying an error message to the user.","usage":{"input_tokens":328957,"output_tokens":3391,"cache_read_input_tokens":276672,"total_tokens":332348},"permission_denials":[]}
